<DocsLayout title="Notes in Haft v9" description="Persist one explicit non-binding fact, observation, caveat, or rationale without turning it into a decision.">
  <h1>Notes</h1>

  <p>
    A Haft note records a non-binding fact, observation, caveat, or small
    rationale. Use <code>h-note</code> when the operator explicitly asks to save
    that material. Ordinary reasoning is not auto-captured.
  </p>

  <h2>Notes are not decisions</h2>

  <p>
    A note can describe a choice or a condition. It cannot bind a choice among
    alternatives, authorize work, approve a specification, or establish that a
    claim is true. Use <code>h-decide</code> for a direct binding choice and
    <code>h-commission</code> for execution authority.
  </p>

  <h2>Record through the typed contract</h2>

  <pre><code>haft interface note.record --json
haft artifact create note.record --input-file input.json --json</code></pre>

  <p>
    The input requires a title. It may carry observations, evidence, rationale,
    anchors, affected files, context, <code>valid_until</code>, search keywords,
    and exact EntityOfConcern coordinates. The kernel validates the payload.
  </p>

  <p>The MCP surface is:</p>

  <pre><code>haft_note(title="...", observations=[...])</code></pre>

  <h2>Typed projection is conditional</h2>

  <p>
    A note may persist without becoming an exact typed
    <code>NoteAtConcern</code> projection. That projection requires both an exact
    <code>entity_ref</code> and its <code>bounded_context_ref</code>. Missing
    coordinates remain visible as underdetermined; Haft does not infer identity
    from names or rank.
  </p>

  <h2>Freshness and later use</h2>

  <p>
    Use <code>valid_until</code> when a receiving use needs a freshness boundary.
    Expiry is an attention signal, not automatic deletion or a claim that the
    historical observation became false.
  </p>

  <p>
    If later work needs a binding choice, create that DecisionRecord through
    its own authority path. Do not "promote" a note by treating its existing
    text as operator approval.
  </p>

